# Agent Keyring — Environment Variables
# Copy this to .env and fill in values, or export them directly.

# ─── Store Selection ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Set KEYRING_GCP_PROJECT to use GCP Secret Manager.
# Leave unset to use the local file store (.secrets.json).
# KEYRING_GCP_PROJECT=your-gcp-project-id

# ─── Local File Store ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the local secrets JSON file.
# Default: .secrets.json in the keyring directory.
# KEYRING_SECRET_STORE=/path/to/.secrets.json

# Root directory for PASTE_FROM: references in .secrets.json.
# Default: 3 directories up from the keyring directory.
# KEYRING_SECRETS_ROOT=/path/to/secrets/parent

# ─── GCP Secret Manager (when KEYRING_GCP_PROJECT is set) ─────
# Path to GCP service account key JSON.
# Falls back to: gcloud ADC, then GCE metadata server.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/sa-key.json
# KEYRING_GCP_SA_KEY=/path/to/sa-key.json

# Prefix for secret names in GCP (avoids collisions in shared projects).
# Default: keyring-
# KEYRING_GCP_PREFIX=keyring-

# Cache TTL for GCP secret values, in seconds.
# Default: 300 (5 minutes). Set to 0 to disable caching.
# KEYRING_GCP_CACHE_TTL=300

# ─── Discovery Tools ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Root directory for secret discovery/migration scripts.
# KEYRING_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/scan
